{"title":"Cashflow Projections: The Numbers Your Business Needs to Work","startsAt":"2026-10-27T18:00:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-27T20:00:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"This session will teach you how to assess your numbers to determine if your business will survive. We will cover:\n\n* Costs of operation\n* What each sale earns after costs\n* How many sales it takes to break even\n* Building a straightforward monthly cash flow projection\n* Setting justifiable prices\n\nWe'll work through the numbers of real businesses together before you begin thinking about your own. No accounting experience required — bring a calculator or your phone.\n\nThe program includes a short networking component, providing participants with an opportunity to connect with other entrepreneurs.\n\nPresented by Ryan Knight, TPL's 2026 [Entrepreneur in Residence](https://tpl.ca/programs-and-classes/featured/entrepreneur-in-residence/) (EIR) at Toronto Reference Library.\n\n**Registration via TPL website:** [https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31](https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31)\n**Drop-ins welcome until room capacity is reached.**\n\nAccessibility\nLive or automated closed captioning, sign language interpretation, intervenor services, or attendant services are available upon request. Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to: [tpl.ca/accessibility-events](https://tpl.ca/accessibility/accessibility-supports/programs-and-events/?_gl=1*v83hy7*_ga*NDk5MDg2NTE1LjE3NjYwMDgxODQ.*_ga_G99DMMNG39*czE3NjkxMDY3NDMkbzE0JGcxJHQxNzY5MTA2ODM0JGozOCRsMCRoMA..).","venue":{"name":"Toronto Public Library - Toronto Reference Library","address":"789 Yonge St, Toronto, ON M4W 2G8, Canada, Toronto","lat":43.671806,"lng":-79.38682,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"Toronto Public Library Small Business Networking Meetup","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/b/6/3/highres_536307491.jpeg"}